<BLCMM v="1">
#<!!!You opened a file saved with BLCMM in FilterTool. Please update to BLCMM to properly open this file!!!>
	<head>
		<type name="TPS" offline="true"/>
		<profiles>
			<profile name="default" current="true"/>
		</profiles>
	</head>
	<body>
		<category name="patch">
			<category name="Credits and Thanks :3">
				<category name="WARNING! Long">
					<comment>TPS Relaunched v.1.0</comment>
					<comment></comment>
					<comment>I've heard the term "Beta Patch" thrown around- I think I'd consider this one of those.</comment>
					<comment>"Created" by WhatLake, after 7 months and half a billion stupid questions in the BL Modding Discord (and plenty of smart answers!)</comment>
					<comment></comment>
					<comment>_____________________________________________________________________________________________________________________</comment>
					<comment></comment>
					<comment>Firstly, a very sincere thanks to all members of the modding community who have allowed me to use or modify code from their own mods:</comment>
					<comment></comment>
					<comment>---Ravenjim and the UCP Team, TPS Community Patch:</comment>
					<comment> </comment>
					<comment>This mod is literally built on the framework that is the TPS UCP, including but hardly limited to the enemy loot pool setup, </comment>
					<comment>a few skill changes (ex. Hyperion Punch), and the entire section "Quality of Life/System Changes- UCP".</comment>
					<comment></comment>
					<comment>The phrase "I couldn't have done it without x" is thrown around a lot but I genuinely wouldn't have known how- or where- to start.</comment>
					<comment></comment>
					<comment></comment>
					<comment>In crediting Ravenjim and the TPS UCP team, it would be unfair to not also credit the people *they* had permission to use code from.</comment>
					<comment></comment>
					<comment>I simply left the UCP file's own credit / thanks section here so it would be crystal clear whose code ended up in this mod.</comment>
					<category name="Community Patch Credits + Thanks ">
						<comment>BL TPS Beta Patch version 2.3 </comment>
						<comment>Made By Jim Raven with ALOT!!! of help from the modding community</comment>
						<comment>Special Thanks to everyone who helped with this project</comment>
						<comment>LightChaosMan 00Schmidt Nikitazed Ugyuu ja_Fortune The_Nocturni</comment>
						<comment>FromDarkHell (old hyperion matching grip/barrel fix) and Apocalyptech for his awesome contributions</comment>
						<comment>ZetaDeamon Uniques drop pools and unique Grinder Recipe</comment>
						<comment>Special thanks for their contribution to the Community to ShadowEvil and LightChaosMan</comment>
					</category>
					<comment>_____________________________________________________________________________________________________________________</comment>
					<comment></comment>
					<comment>---Rayjiun + The 2.5 Team, Borderlands 2.5:</comment>
					<comment></comment>
					<comment>2.5 was rhe first BL2 overhaul I ever downloaded, and I started to learn bits and pieces about BLCMM modding from reverse engineering it. </comment>
					<comment>Simply put, it opened my mind to how...weirdly possible...it could be make a mod that transforms one of my favorite games.</comment>
					<comment></comment>
					<comment>All of the changes in the "Quality of Life/ System Changes- BL2.5 + Plasma Enriched" section minus the Coop Leveling code are from 2.5, </comment>
					<comment>and the manner in which I created unique weapon skins is basically just what I think 2.5 did, though the actual results are my own.</comment>
					<comment></comment>
					<comment></comment>
					<comment>_____________________________________________________________________________________________________________________</comment>
					<comment></comment>
					<comment>---Plasmasnack, BL2/Plasma Enriched:</comment>
					<comment></comment>
					<comment>Firstly, shoutout to Bl2 Enriched itself for being a sick-ass BL2 mod! </comment>
					<comment>When I used to peruse and try out BL2 overhauls, this one stood out as particularly tactful- a great balance of simple and fun.</comment>
					<comment></comment>
					<comment>One thing this mod did that I don't see a lot do is individually rebalance nonunique weapon and shield types- </comment>
					<comment></comment>
					<comment>Relaunched uses a similar layout for its own weapon and shield balancing but very different stats.</comment>
					<comment></comment>
					<comment>While I doubt I'm the first modder since Enriched's release to change and organize those sorts of values, that's where I got the idea from.</comment>
					<comment></comment>
					<comment>Thanks for the A-okay on that!</comment>
					<comment>_____________________________________________________________________________________________________________________</comment>
					<comment></comment>
					<comment>---PawnM0v3, Azurelands </comment>
					<comment></comment>
					<comment>Before I learned that Azurelands was built off of BL2.5, I bothered Pawn about using a bunch of what was ultimately BL2.5 code.</comment>
					<comment></comment>
					<comment>Thanks for being patient about that!</comment>
					<comment></comment>
					<comment></comment>
					<comment>If anyone involved in the creation of any mods that I received permission to use code from has an issue with that inclusion, or any others, please let me know! </comment>
					<comment></comment>
					<comment>I want to ensure everyone is properly credited for their work, no matter how many layers of overhauls is goes through.</comment>
					<comment></comment>
					<comment>_____________________________________________________________________________________________________________________</comment>
					<comment></comment>
					<comment>---Zetademon, BLModded114, apple1417, mopoid and everyone else who helped when I had bizarre or basic questions</comment>
					<comment></comment>
					<comment>Thank all of you for the patience and advice! Not easy to help out a guy who does not know the slightest thing about coding.</comment>
					<comment></comment>
					<comment>_____________________________________________________________________________________________________________________</comment>
					<comment></comment>
					<comment>Finally, a very special thanks to my playtesters! I had playtesters! :0</comment>
					<comment></comment>
					<comment></comment>
					<comment>---PhyrexianGrace, especially in the fledgling stages of the mod</comment>
					<comment></comment>
					<comment></comment>
					<comment>---Tanya, especially for starting fresh characters while I focused on UVHM and helping to make sure coop was playable.</comment>
					<comment></comment>
					<comment>Noticed a LOT of things that didn't even cross my mind in the early stages.</comment>
					<comment></comment>
					<comment></comment>
					<comment>---Two of my personal friends, who had a weird amount of faith in this project. </comment>
					<comment></comment>
					<comment>I don't know if I would have had the confidence to publicly release this without their kind words. </comment>
					<comment></comment>
					<comment>Thanks, everyone!</comment>
					<comment></comment>
					<comment></comment>
					<comment>And, if you've managed to sift through this wall of yellow text, thanks for installing my mod (and presumably reading some of my blabbering)!</comment>
					<comment></comment>
					<comment>I really hope you enjoy what I've put together.</comment>
				</category>
			</category>
			<category name="How Do You Know If It's Running?">
				<comment>You'll know the mod is active if it says " BL TPS Re-Launched 1.0 " at the bottom of the BA Rank screen. Fingers crossed!</comment>
				<hotfix name="Name" level="None">
					<code profiles="default">set WillowGame.Default__BadassPanelGFxObject TooltipsText_Redeem <font color="#9f99ff"> Running TPS Re-Launched 1.0</font> <br></code>
					<code profiles="default">set WillowGame.Default__BadassPanelGFxObject TooltipsText_Close <StringAliasMap:GFx_Cancel> Close</code>
					<code profiles="default">set WillowGame.Default__BadassPanelGFxObject TooltipsText_ActivateBonusStats <StringAliasMap:GFx_Accept> Redeem Token &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<StringAliasMap:GFx_Y> Enable Bonus Stats</code>
					<code profiles="default">set WillowGame.Default__BadassPanelGFxObject TooltipsText_DeactivateBonusStats <StringAliasMap:GFx_Accept> Redeem Token &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<StringAliasMap:GFx_Y> Disable Bonus Stats</code>
				</hotfix>
			</category>
			<category name="Fundamental UCP Code ">
				<category name="GBX hotfixes">
