						<category name="All The Guns ">
							<hotfix name="Claptrap" package="GD_Prototype_Streaming">
								<code profiles="default">set GD_Prototype_Skills.Fragmented.AllTheGuns:AttributePresentationDefinition_3 Description <font size="15">Gun Damage: $NUMBER$</font></code>
								<code profiles="default">set GD_Prototype_Skills.Fragmented.AllTheGuns:AttributePresentationDefinition_2 Description <font size="15">Fire Rate: $NUMBER$<br>Reload Speed: $NUMBER$</font></code>
								<code profiles="default">set GD_Prototype_Skills.Fragmented.AllTheGuns:AttributePresentationDefinition_0 Description <font size="15">Wrong Type Damage: $NUMBER$</font></code>
								<code profiles="default">set GD_Prototype_Skills.Fragmented.AllTheGuns:AttributePresentationDefinition_1 Description <font size="15">Matching Type Ammo Regeneration: Up to $NUMBER$ of Max Ammo / sec</font></code>
								<code profiles="default">set GD_Prototype_Skills.Fragmented.AllTheGuns SkillDescription <font size="15">[skill]Gun Subroutines.[-skill] You randomly pick a [skill]Subroutine[-skill] focused on a Gun type, improving several stats with that type, but [useful]penalizing[-useful] the rest.<br>Upon selecting a [skill]Subroutine[-skill] you gain [corrosive]100[-corrosive] [skill]Frag Stacks[-skill], which decay over time. When you run out of [skill]Frag Stacks[-skill], your [skill]Subroutine[-skill] will be replaced with a new one.<br>Note: [skill]Rocket Launchers[-skill] do not receive the [skill]Ammo Regeneration[-skill] bonus.</font></code>
